41dcb469733a570245c29"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-94-23","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":94,"verse":23,"english":"He that does not slay a physician skilled in ways and means, a servant given to enlisting the sympathies of his fellow-servants against his master, or a hero that covets riches, is slain (by them).","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.764,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-100-27"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2094023","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"63025e4f42d9f01304b82ccf0a4102ad28f275b173d9034a89933002ae0b4b71","compact":"7bde0b400f1b0fad88235b4cd6798707498cff8527402d7c0fcfc11b7201b889","nasal":"f141f31c2c96c1787ecfec1183787746d0c4f6d6c4a0938a1432012b700c4f5c"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-94-24","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":94,"verse":24,"english":"And had you chosen for your general one that is confident, is endowed with intelligence and fortitude, sprung in a respectable race, and attached and able?","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.884,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-100-28"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2094024","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"68cf28c6eed4f37639b4727966d9d6739b104140565771a9b093044b5d9508a3","compact":"3abde3125e9f763286d0b6fbafd4db082a9e61841c442d690dc994cb5c54570d","nasal":"3abde3125e9f763286d0b6fbafd4db082a9e61841c442d690dc994cb5c54570d"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-94-25","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":94,"verse":25,"english":"And do you practically honour your foremost warriors possessed of prowess, who have already given evidence of their manliness?","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-100-29"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2094025","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"2ddc1e2ef0b7f982405271941cf92d6c4be003360a63dcc63d72f278b8b6403b","compact":"f649898a44554030526308eca8a320af766f24fef31daf77fc6a913b9b7b2c76","nasal":"020d31dbce6f05be64907fb91ac535ef0a78dee5aaf2a079635a0d09ce593465"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-94-26","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":94,"verse":26,"english":"And do you at the proper time grant your soldiers what you should, provision and pay; and do not delay in doing this?","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.842,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-100-30"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2094026","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"a18d528c7dc51c74280953688e931b3dd5c2dac42dda9ffbdfaf0802cbe0b0fa","compact":"f5ec98b72abcaf75ab8b86dcc0e2c6ba9d823aa8321843e2d8dae66af51aaf88","nasal":"6135dfb361d87e674521549c4b932e5d420d4f4d0b8709b49da3cf4e9af0216d"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-94-27","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":94,"verse":27,"english":"If the proper time for granting provision and pay be passed, the servants get wroth with their master and tax him; and great is the evil that springs herefrom.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.507,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-100-31"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2094027","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"be607b4fb1911cc868a302eeb28c2aabf97db187e532b70f0c27a48497725cce","compact":"823a5f94cd221fa797994837f80075054001d5ee7cab4f7d360994b0dfef4c06","nasal":"b6d65cdbd5e4b539f318c2a840cf3725ed2e1e723432816285042a7970f251a3"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-94-28","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":94,"verse":28,"english":"And are the principal descendants of our race attached to you; and are they, when enlisted on your side with concentrated minds, ready to lay down their lives?","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-100-32"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2094028","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"7e0566a1c4e91cdb7e0c0d2df071592d161b5694af7440a26be918dec30260a7","compact":"753f9fe2579a0c792e2475f0e9cef72302c39381d451fcbfd595cff31039b0c1","nasal":"a4fc8727990c2e9a5003a6faa7aaaf53edf6dff4181591caaeab2f9434497228"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-94-29","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":94,"verse":29,"english":"O Bharata, are your spies persons coming from the provinces, and learned, upright, endowed with presence of mind, representing the truth, and possessed of wisdon?","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-100-33"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2094029","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"11d3dca5be3723eda26c00327675715f52c538dd68f4adc0204e10354961d114","compact":"a6386c6522415192356931ae2837ed442e0d6678ec7df7f09e109ec6684764d3","nasal":"719db9efe9406856f80f7ebb9db85ba2c621aa442f5ab975d51602be8ef2f63e"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-94-30","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":94,"verse":30,"english":"And do you acquire intelligence of the expedients, eighteen* in respect of others, and fifteen in respect of the own self, by means of every three spies appointed in connection with each of these expedients, men quite ignorant of each other's counsels? *1. Minister. 2. Priest. 3. Heir-apparent. 4. General. 5. Warder. 6. Gatekeeper of the inner-apartment. 7. Jailer. 8. Treasurer. 9. Conveyer of the royal orders. 10. Pleaders. 11. Judges. 12. Members of the council. 13. Distributor of pay and provision to the army. 14. Journeymen. 15. Justice of the peace. 16. Protector of the frontiers of the kingdom. 17. Magistrate. 18. Guards of rivers, hills, and fortresses.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.806,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-100-34"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2094030","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"068372c790ef93897c4232ef965d45f7970990b40addafc56c0763a838f316e6","compact":"edd00a41204d24ac0c5c81469a783d010b63bc38d673fc008a0f4dc56fe90096","nasal":"b7548de17559a45a1ca40c7334fc0c5695b042a489c3af2416620fe84fe9f1fe"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-94-31","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":94,"verse":31,"english":"And do you not contemn those. weak ones that, O destroyer of your. foes, having been expelled, have come again (to you)?","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-100-35"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2094031","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"e0db9b254e5c05c647f8b0eaf825bbf4f4dbd5132ac002a79ea13a9fe7c8d396","compact":"05508755b5064fc2c7406e9bb041daabc53076226822c7cd83c131289d1ddc84","nasal":"05508755b5064fc2c7406e9bb041daabc53076226822c7cd83c131289d1ddc84"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-94-32","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":94,"verse":32,"english":"And, my child, you did not minister to atheistical Brāhmaṇas? These childish persons proud of their learning are only fit for bringing evils upon others. While there are excellent scriptures, these people of subtle intellects, having acquired a knowledge of dialectics, speak vanities.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-100-36"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2094032","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"9de3226f5f71f02d76bf61bad93c921b12bd80278816fa81660879167fee0a75","compact":"8b516253c76839180551f3356003d4e5b7049e5fc3152fc702c2653d8fdfdc76","nasal":"47ec3e78908af3a0af8b312beeabb66fd4fc4b574b879d6d53881a6915aaceac"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-94-33","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":94,"verse":33,"english":"And, my child, you did not minister to atheistical Brāhmaṇas? These childish persons proud of their learning are only fit for bringing evils upon others. While there are excellent scriptures, these people of subtle intellects, having acquired a knowledge of dialectics, speak vanities.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.899,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-100-36"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2094033","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"e48a37aa176275464dcfdc3bda19e5a50080adc54cd344fd4d138c03ebc515cf","compact":"6639b4816d86b348b57610fdc4148a63662ceef132d1cee923fd2468ee324753","nasal":"b4985639235694043e5b6d3b2e189bec5307b34028924b46d386529efed05bac"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-94-34","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":94,"verse":34,"english":"My child, do you protect the prosperous and renowned Ayodhyā, inhabited formerly by our heroic predecessors; bearing a true name; having strong gates; filled with elephants, steeds, and cars; thronged by thousands; with noble Brāhmaṇas, Kștriyas and Vaisyas breathing high spirits, and with their senses controlled, each engaged in his own task; abounding in people learned in the Veda; and surrounded with palatial mansions of various shapes?","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.882,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-100-37"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2094034","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"989b68bbd1804a956ac21446c634fa72f00186a29c549ddac182dd4ceb025762","compact":"d2ef8a686e78345ad87ab6474f9b8bdc11f0dcb44fd2ec28dd04779e7d6d13fa","nasal":"d2ef8a686e78345ad87ab6474f9b8bdc11f0dcb44fd2ec28dd04779e7d6d13fa"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-94-35","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":94,"verse":35,"english":"My child, do you protect the prosperous and renowned Ayodhyā, inhabited formerly by our heroic predecessors; bearing a true name; having strong gates; filled with elephants, steeds, and cars; thronged by thousands; with noble Brāhmaṇas, Kștriyas and Vaisyas breathing high spirits, and with their senses controlled, each engaged in his own task; abounding in people learned in the Veda; and surrounded with palatial mansions of various shapes?","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.9,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-100-37"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2094035","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"0e6372d0c824c5b6e4221d318fe5478862a1092cb091b422c59ff8d66ae7f17c","compact":"a60aa9085023e1a38f2a54b5e9a317f7b3aebcfe5f339936396b294e512abdbc","nasal":"282a5431c1ce77eb4e548fd983bc9f7b7beb5fe3de9a70234236c75c826c4096"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-94-36","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":94,"verse":36,"english":"My child, do you protect the prosperous and renowned Ayodhyā, inhabited formerly by our heroic predecessors; bearing a true name; having strong gates; filled with elephants, steeds, and cars; thronged by thousands; with noble Brāhmaṇas, Kștriyas and Vaisyas breathing high spirits, and with their senses controlled, each engaged in his own task; abounding in people learned in the Veda; and surrounded with palatial mansions of various shapes?","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.986,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-100-37"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2094036","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"e087c188d2319f04f1db84f269d3895291cc421fe4ccac8f446d2e61e918b4cb","compact":"3b19deb255900fc5c2c83adaece2daa2cf9caf25443245cfd7690dfead1a6c52","nasal":"3b19deb255900fc5c2c83adaece2daa2cf9caf25443245cfd7690dfead1a6c52"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-94-37","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":94,"verse":37,"english":"And, O descendant of Raghu, are the flourishing provinces marked with hundreds of Chaityas, filled with prosperous people, graced with abodes of deities, places for distributing water, and tanks, with man and women in happy mood, gay with meetings and festivities, having their outskirts well furrowed, provided with beasts, void of ill feelings, depending on tanks for their water supply, charming, renounced by fierce animals, free from all kinds of fear, decked with mines, left by unrighteous people, and well governed by my predecessors, having a good time of it?","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.912,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-100-38"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2094037","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"52991f7fc17c7a8407c17e2b007a11a03f80d211c8129e5576431b5941ed1866","compact":"147c4abc34034726ceaca37e32f658920e171736d69710f4d70c0bbfd87fda57","nasal":"147c4abc34034726ceaca37e32f658920e171736d69710f4d70c0bbfd87fda57"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-94-38","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":94,"verse":38,"english":"And, O descendant of Raghu, are the flourishing provinces marked with hundreds of Chaityas, filled with prosperous people, graced with abodes of deities, places for distributing water, and tanks, with man and women in happy mood, gay with meetings and festivities, having their outskirts well furrowed, provided with beasts, void of ill feelings, depending on tanks for their water supply, charming, renounced by fierce animals, free from all kinds of fear, decked with mines, left by unrighteous people, and well governed by my predecessors, having a good time of it?","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.881,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-100-38"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2094038","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"24918ccd9b3b94673f3bd4f38ee11485c06a8d0abc90a6bf86f58b15ae1bc3b6","compact":"a029557f13197140dee7c3855f63eb8cd9de052104489911afe3dad09e4e5fb3","nasal":"a029557f13197140dee7c3855f63eb8cd9de052104489911afe3dad09e4e5fb3"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-94-39","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":94,"verse":39,"english":"And, O descendant of Raghu, are the flourishing provinces marked with hundreds of Chaityas, filled with prosperous people, graced with abodes of deities, places for distributing water, and tanks, with man and women in happy mood, gay with meetings and festivities, having their outskirts well furrowed, provided with beasts, void of ill feelings, depending on tanks for their water supply, charming, renounced by fierce animals, free from all kinds of fear, decked with mines, left by unrighteous people, and well governed by my predecessors, having a good time of it?","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.946,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-100-38"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2094039","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"86ce8604bbb0f7b442d097d6614d67e3564a789b14618c7d7e476abde2eb3b82","compact":"8dec63d98b7d107ae1ab3ead38e01f367ee0c09e5a07e1ccdfa3ac966c5ad5e0","nasal":"8dec63d98b7d107ae1ab3ead38e01f367ee0c09e5a07e1ccdfa3ac966c5ad5e0"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-94-40","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":94,"verse":40,"english":"And do agriculturists and cow herds find favour in your sight? And remaining in their respective vocations, do they enjoy happiness?","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.859,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-100-39"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2094040","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"0899080fb2e7be2bcba17b235dc417e76797cdc69a55ca8dbd15580c08cf6554","compact":"8fe028a2ad484e3370d3060cfe3967c76eb0aab616d72fa66f9dcd206dc3b005","nasal":"8fe028a2ad484e3370d3060cfe3967c76eb0aab616d72fa66f9dcd206dc3b005"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-94-41","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":94,"verse":41,"english":"And do you maintain them by securing to them what they wish for and removing from them what they wish away? All the dwellers in his dominions should be protected by the king.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-100-40"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2094041","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"561006dea73808fb7dcde2ea122082d0ee836213448653e2352f0399239f9393","compact":"015a1f3b6053a15f1b21929374497b35b1d792b79283f2902a9396482b3272c2","nasal":"015a1f3b6053a15f1b21929374497b35b1d792b79283f2902a9396482b3272c2"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-94-42","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":94,"verse":42,"english":"And do you conciliate the females; and are they well protected by you? And do you not regard them; and do you not open to them your mind?","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.78,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-100-41"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2094042","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"e2725e4f5513a6977200b07cfa1830daf9aafa427d1ec5bc2b13382a5a40ac5c","compact":"4ad67c6ef8e99856b3bd534a20b351e4c73f31d9a5d48f9b98a8be3379f35865","nasal":"28201c6e4d943afeeac50008a553dea641e612480a993acb752091f58811b694"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-94-43","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":94,"verse":43,"english":"And do you show yourself daily in the court, well robed? And rising in the morning, do you show yourself in the high-ways?","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.396,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-100-43"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2094043","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"708ba56fc9321d4c08f1bed5138613ece42bd58f90899d25c78922d7005db927","compact":"eeb47fc9d06a6ca887a27d360add5e91881ecef25567b7b0dc3e79b5cb4babdc","nasal":"ce215cea170ff2d65e5a5cd98910f87770297881477309b10fa3200487125e59"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-94-44","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":94,"verse":44,"english":"Are all the forts furnished with wealth, corn, arms water, machines, artisans, and bowmen?","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.543,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-100-45"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2094044","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"54feac9e6d550c739fc439c5b5d1472b294868dcf19f792b34929fa3f80de39b","compact":"c74e26b5b3d20713f3d422decaba9642246a741062a81d75f339b6dc407797a0","nasal":"3a1e17257b26cc86de5437b67cc30541c2483e3171640d655d4b935c5cd445a5"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-94-45","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":94,"verse":45,"english":"And are your incomings great and outgoings slender? And, O Raghu's descendant, you do not give away your coffers to the undeserving?","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.871,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-100-46"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2094045","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"c102a885ee8810e3c89b8d2443c52878afa7560015ef24de7c3fd1031fa8710f","compact":"ae7cf4bf3a5e37b01eb573ff219070c492ae23da056f2fceb6586595ba33d86b","nasal":"ae7cf4bf3a5e37b01eb573ff219070c492ae23da056f2fceb6586595ba33d86b"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-94-46","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":94,"verse":46,"english":"And did you spend your wealth in the interests of the deities, or the pitris, or the Brāhmaṇas who have come to you, or warriors, or friends?","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-100-47"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2094046","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"52825b949248aece280d1392c428377738d1cbf0bc6fc40c87fe2787ed291c63","compact":"77df8271eebee931fc467ad3b2c62fb7237847777df0a5448c4c4b2fb1b5460e","nasal":"77df8271eebee931fc467ad3b2c62fb7237847777df0a5448c4c4b2fb1b5460e"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-94-47","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":94,"verse":47,"english":"If any respectable, pure-spirited and clean person happen to be accused by some one of theft or other crimes, do you from covetousness punish him without first having him tried by persons versed in scripture?","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.658,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-100-48"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2094047","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"a1847ce748b89e8f73d48afb53139e2e89ab70e33f5276484c083221216f7ffc","compact":"36beb168b972c0ddfaa2543635d534e38177e5bd41f9eaaad480a154285a4e3c","nasal":"36beb168b972c0ddfaa2543635d534e38177e5bd41f9eaaad480a154285a4e3c"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-94-48","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":94,"verse":48,"english":"And, O best of men, is a thief, that has been caught, interrogated (as to his guilt), and found with the stolen property on his person, set free (by your men) from motives of gain.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.617,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-100-49"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2094048","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"83915df347023ffd45c844bbb88fedda1c15717f7ce711ee953f72695b07bac5","compact":"d3adc729942e27f695a0e04983c02a3277a8f581135373d09e6205b37a5874fa","nasal":"1c345b67b520fb28b6f1f4d23fb91737882d2fd7a03d2e7aace7fff6a75f7e55"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-94-49","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":94,"verse":49,"english":"And do your counsellors, o descendant of Raghu, accomplished in various lore, uninfluenced by greed, consider the conduct of both the rich and the poor involved in peril?","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.746,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-100-50"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2094049","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"b8daaf9b571187f18c757a96bfdbe6be33833ea0284026cd4275369798e7cf85","compact":"7fa90a7d01c91ce9b7edc9b4734aa1823f5773290776df389452d9b966a987d9","nasal":"9da7060508f38afe7055ffa05f85be2739f504347e5802cf64aa8ba477fb9a52"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-94-50","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":94,"verse":50,"english":"O son of the Raghu race, the tears of those who have been falsely charged with any offence, (and who have failed to obtain justice), dropping, destroy the sons as well as the beasts of the ruler that minds his own comfort only.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.841,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-100-51"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2094050","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"e9c3a46494cba6c688f1265689a267c4cc8a99240a699b63b725e39740309d28","compact":"ab22907ee3ac000a18ee1f51fb6971ca23ae1f701c6dcb54431276c804d3a7e4","nasal":"b463922b51de4706016ab883895ff3b433ab0da40f90e06acc03142315da6e6d"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-94-51","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":94,"verse":51,"english":"And do you with these three, gifts, mind and word, try to win over aged people, boys, physicians, and the principal ones?","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.776,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-100-52"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2094051","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"0c89d943e4d913d7e6d14f9551d3d79923b9559cc49cf544e6e11271bdbd1d59","compact":"d212efbc3b0f1165a05835ba021026ad4077309933dee790890f57b54833374d","nasal":"d212efbc3b0f1165a05835ba021026ad4077309933dee790890f57b54833374d"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-94-52","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":94,"verse":52,"english":"And do you salute spiritual preceptors, aged persons, ascetics, gods, guests, Caityas, emancipated one, and Brāhmaṇās?","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.906,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-100-53"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2094052","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"d4bec8035737b33a222958dae7ba5909c7addb572e65ffec22cc71cbdfa7b95a","compact":"fe09ae9308c8ffdcd1dbfbe0672780fb2dc99daf69092e2ceca44f81d48d9cfa","nasal":"48c39546517321f2abccc3d26060018cf902fc26223d255691996bb3e841551c"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-94-53","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":94,"verse":53,"english":"And you do not oppose righteousness by interest, or interest by virtue, or both by desire, intent on gratifying the senses?","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.789,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-100-54"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2094053","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"a1e4eceaf0322a089a52bb6e8a61babe657f99cf0def2ceaf20af031fe94721b","compact":"188601064587693b5a40755940f886b6a4ac774b2cb8a37cb8d5bffa410ce092","nasal":"188601064587693b5a40755940f886b6a4ac774b2cb8a37cb8d5bffa410ce092"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-94-54","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":94,"verse":54,"english":"And, O foremost of conquerors, do you, O you cognisant of time, in season resorting to interest, desire, and virtue respectively, attain them, O bestower of boons?","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.585,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-100-55"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2094054","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"ce2e3ba7c595cba66015941c58e497704e4c9c10468bb3f898af264ee3d73086","compact":"14c9f7a2739388f1cf7e32e2ed331e8318bdd21e61a85d1242cf2acbcdf06c33","nasal":"14c9f7a2739388f1cf7e32e2ed331e8318bdd21e61a85d1242cf2acbcdf06c33"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-94-55","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":94,"verse":55,"english":"And do Brāhmaṇas versed in all religious lore and knowing interest, together with the citizens and the inhabitants of the provinces wish for your happiness, O highly wise one?","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.776,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-100-56"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2094055","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"f017c97da0eb7f0697510f7cab7d248412da9b3e41c7322aaa581f84f95f5d45","compact":"9e46fcec8973f0b67116ce40c1d019e09e01b151c3768dec9b85fc25f9a0735e","nasal":"d47027c590c5e23b7a0049930e58f64e10ccae181a3c1e461f7201a850a8fde1"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-94-56","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":94,"verse":56,"english":"Atheism, untruthfulness, inattention, anger, procrastination, companionship with evil persons, indolence, gratification of the senses, consultation with a single person concerning the needs of a kingdom, taking counsel with those that are cognisant of evils alone, omission to take in hand a task that has been decided upon, divulgence of counsel, non-commencement of a course in the morning, and marching against all the foes at one and the same time, have you eschewed these ten and four faults?","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-100-57"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2094056","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"0114c2d70158c57a83de7c5821d0455908812c781a713bb36b864bbd1191a3bd","compact":"5bfe6c05683f9a59785e7943952457ab9f494ebf6e6eeb05a8f9ee7476a8b49f","nasal":"e06f044606c4913e0be23852e127d325b47847f4405cbb982b4b879d60ae570c"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-94-57","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":94,"verse":57,"english":"Atheism, untruthfulness, inattention, anger, procrastination, companionship with evil persons, indolence, gratification of the senses, consultation with a single person concerning the needs of a kingdom, taking counsel with those that are cognisant of evils alone, omission to take in hand a task that has been decided upon, divulgence of counsel, non-commencement of a course in the morning, and marching against all the foes at one and the same time, have you eschewed these ten and four faults?","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.896,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-100-57"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2094057","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"ca34fbe6044565ae6cbe53efee5e27e0ca4174510f39ba3cb585861842760e1c","compact":"46202ddab3e901dbbd1a29929526dc0ff1620234239caa29e707088ce62d5cf4","nasal":"8309290267b274a7f68752ce3960a49e28e6c6843388882b0c53940510d1b10c"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-94-58","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":94,"verse":58,"english":"Atheism, untruthfulness, inattention, anger, procrastination, companionship with evil persons, indolence, gratification of the senses, consultation with a single person concerning the needs of a kingdom, taking counsel with those that are cognisant of evils alone, omission to take in hand a task that has been decided upon, divulgence of counsel, non-commencement of a course in the morning, and marching against all the foes at one and the same time, have you eschewed these ten and four faults?","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.761,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-100-57"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2094058","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"c258456245b3ceb553795c16803bc0e7f768f74545abc57d2171e39733aa60f1","compact":"8b0295eb2457d04e2afabf07b121567d797573107bdeed0e47679a4e07b9946e","nasal":"9460a175c8d0f351efac6d012272d2fc5052bc33a9898fff7fa1b9e88c68e345"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-94-59","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":94,"verse":59,"english":"And, O son of Raghu, you do not alone partake of sapid meats yourself alone? And do you share them with those friends who expect it?","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.886,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-100-63"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2094059","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"3986f482e8c2f0d21e73df197ae58cce22029c64ee1dfa0323703e5d172ed429","compact":"c310ebbbd4a7d4b038af6d940a907c551128798ad2128e00cb6c38065698a246","nasal":"c310ebbbd4a7d4b038af6d940a907c551128798ad2128e00cb6c38065698a246"}}]
